WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:06.020
When season 1 of The Witcher dropped on Netflix
back in December 2019, it was an instant smash

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.020
hit.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.950
While there were some differences between
the series and the video games, most fans

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.920
believed it to be a faithful adaptation of
author Andrzej Sapkowski's books upon which

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.850
the CD Projekt Red games are based.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:20.439
A standout for many viewers was the brilliant
casting of Superman actor Henry Cavill in

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:22.490
the lead role of Geralt of Rivia.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:26.179
The show follows Geralt — as well as the
sorceress Yennefer of Vengerberg and the Crown

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:29.999
Princess Ciri — as they go through various
events at different points in time, based

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:33.290
heavily on Sapkowski's The Last Wish and Sword
of Destiny.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:36.670
Their characters go through formative events
that shape them into the legends they are

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.649
to become until all of their stories eventually
merge.

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:43.489
The first season was well-received by critics
and audiences alike, and expectations are

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:48.109
high going into season 2 — especially after
the overwhelming season 1 finale, appropriately

00:00:48.109 --> 00:00:49.730
titled "Much More."

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:53.370
While fans are eager to see the continuing
adventures of Geralt and friends, some unfortunate

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.210
news has emerged from the production.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.789
According to sources close to The Witcher's
production, Cavill has suffered injuries that

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:02.170
have sidelined him for the moment — although
filming has still continued for scenes that

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.350
don't include him.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:07.040
As detailed in a report first published by
The Sun and later in follow-up coverage from

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.420
Deadline, Cavill suffered a leg injury while
he was shooting something at Arborfield Studios

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.650
in London.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.130
Reports indicate that Cavill was doing his
own stunts 20 feet into the air while wearing

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.530
a safety harness, and that's when the injury
took place.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:23.189
The expectation is that Cavill will remain
sidelined for "a short period of time" while

00:01:23.189 --> 00:01:26.660
production on The Witcher continues shooting
scenes that don't require him.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:30.340
The Sun published quotes from an anonymous
source who described how the injury transpired:

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.920
"The filming has been hit because of what
happened to Henry.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.060
He was on an assault course and injured his
leg.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.960
He just suddenly pulled up and was clearly
in a lot of pain.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:42.200
It wasn't clear if an object had hit his leg
or it was some sort of hamstring or muscle

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.200
injury.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.939
[...] It wasn't bad enough to need an ambulance,
but it's messed up the filming schedule as

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.000
he can't walk properly.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.840
He has to wear heavy [armor] in the scenes
and he just wouldn't be able to do it with

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.840
his leg injury."

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.610
Similar to many other productions, The Witcher
is expected to go on a hiatus for the holidays

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:59.590
later in December, so production would stop
soon regardless of what happened to Cavill.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.549
With the extra time off, hopefully Cavill
has plenty of time to rest up and enter production

00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:05.560
in 2021 feeling good and healthy.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.610
2020 has been a rough year for residents of
the Kingdom of Cintra.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.850
As was the case with most film and television
productions this year, The Witcher had to

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:16.030
halt filming as a result of the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.500
Not only did this push things back, but it
also made it so that not everyone from the

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.800
first season could come back to reprise their
roles.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:26.280
Thue Rasmussen , who played Eskel on The Witcher
season 1, had to drop out of the second season

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.520
due to scheduling conflicts that came about
from the coronavirus delay.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.830
The COVID-19 pandemic also hit particularly
close to home for The Witcher cast and crew

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:37.790
when actor Kristofer Hivju tested positive
for the disease back in March.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.400
The pause in filming first began in March
and lasted until August.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.730
Filming resumed for a little while before
halting again in November after several more

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.360
positive COVID-19 cases came about within
the production.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.849
It's been touch and go for The Witcher for
almost an entire year now, and hopefully once

00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:55.390
production gets back on its feet with Cavill
in the saddle again, things will go smoothly

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:56.540
from there on out.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.610
Fortunately, the production is able to carry
on without Cavill for the time being, so fingers

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.220
crossed that things won't get pushed back
too much.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.780
As of right now, The Witcher season 2 is slated
to come out sometime in 2021, but keep checking

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.379
back to Looper as more details emerge in the
coming months.

